  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNODC Institutional Transparency and Citizen Participation at municipal levels - Transparency at municipal levels</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNODC Institutionell transparens och medborgarinflytande p&#xe5; kommunal niv&#xe5;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective 1: Number of Autonomous Municipal Governments have reduced their levels of corruption risks in at least 12 identified areas.
Objective 2:&#xa0;Organized civil society, with emphasis on women&apos;s organizations, is empowered to exercise its right to social control in the beneficiary municipalities.&#xa0;
Objective 3: Culture of transparency and integrity has been promoted in the targeted municipalities.
new Objective 4: An official Bolivian data base on species of plants and animals living in Bolivian forests has been produced.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att st&#xe4;rka en kultur av transparens och minska korruptionen i 60 utvalda kommuner genom att st&#xe4;rka den tekniska kompetensen f&#xf6;r de kvinnor och m&#xe4;n som arbetar i kommunerna vad avser effektiv kommunal f&#xf6;rvaltning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNODC has applied to Sida for funding of 18 million SEK to carry out the &quot;Institutional Transparency and       Citizen Participation at municipal levels&quot; in 60 selected Bolivian municipalities, during the period June 2017 &#x2013; March 2020.

The idea behind the present proposal is that selected municipalities will start promoting a culture of transparency, while receiving technical assistance to improve the municipal officials&apos; skills in order to deliver more efficient services to their communities. Also, civil society organisations, especially led by women, will also receive technical assistance to enhance their social control capabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
